# --- ATOMIC GIT ENGINE COMMIT TEMPLATE ---
# Format: <type>(<scope>): <short description in present imperative>
#
# <type> must be one of:
#   feat     : A new feature
#   fix      : A bug fix
#   refactor : Code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   perf     : Performance improvement
#   test     : Adding missing or correcting existing tests
#   docs     : Documentation changes only
#   style    : Formatting, white-space, commas (no production code change)
#   chore    : Tooling, dependencies, maintenance tasks
#   build    : Build system or packaging changes
#   ci       : CI/CD configuration files and scripts
#   security : Vulnerability fix or security hardening
#   revert   : Reverts a previous commit
#
# <scope> is optional (e.g., auth, api, ui, config, db, test, git)
#
# Rules:
#   1. One independent logical change per atomic commit.
#   2. Subject line maximum 100 characters.
#   3. Use imperative, present tense ("add", not "added" or "adds").
#   4. Do NOT end the subject line with a period.
#   5. Never use generic titles like "update", "wip", "changes", "fix".
#
# --- Optional Body (Explain WHAT and WHY, not HOW) ---
#
# --- Optional Footer (Breaking changes, issue references) ---
# BREAKING CHANGE: <description>
# Closes #<issue_number>

